<title>USA: Copley gets Procainamide HCl ANDA okay.</title>
<headline>Copley gets Procainamide HCl ANDA okay.</headline>
<dateline>CANTON, Mass. 1996-12-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Copley Pharmaceutical Inc said that the U.S. Food and Drug Administration has given its approval of the company's Abbreviated New Drug Application (ANDA) to manufacture and market Procainamide Hydrochloride (HCl) Extended-Release Tablets in the 1000 milligrams (mg) strength.</p>
<p>Copley said this product strength joins Copley's existing line of procainamide HCl tablets in the 500 mg and 750 mg strengths.</p>
<p>Procainamide HCl is a cardiovascular prescription drug used to treat life-threatening ventricular arrythmias, atrial fibrillation, and paroxysmal atrial tachycardia.</p>
</text>
